feat(editor): right-click format document/selection with per-extension formatter detection

- New formatter registry (src/modules/editor/lib/formatter.ts): maps file
  extensions to prettier parsers (js/jsx/ts/tsx, json/jsonc/json5,
  html/htm/vue, css/scss/less, md/markdown/mdx, yml/yaml, graphql/gql)
  with in-process prettier 3 via dynamic import - plugins are code-split
  so only the used language parser loads
- Python (.py) formats via black through the one-shot shell runner:
  temp file in the file own directory so pyproject.toml config applies;
  cleaned up in a finally block
- EditorPane right-click menu (EditorFormatMenu): Format Document always,
  Format Selection when text is selected; names the formatter + extension,
  disabled no-formatter row for unsupported types
- Selection formatting splices only the selected range, keeps it selected
  after formatting, trims prettier trailing newline, and falls back to
  whole-document formatting when the fragment is not parseable in
  isolation (JSON slices, partial HTML trees)
- Whole-doc formatting skips the dispatch entirely when nothing changed
  (no dirty flag / undo step for no-op formats)
- Version 1.5.0
